* ZENO 1.1 If you are reading this to find out how to win - STOP!!!
BEGINNER
$ DISK BEGINNER
$ FILE HELP
* Sample HELP Program - CCS
say Some of the commands available are:
say List to type a list of the files on a disk
say Type to type a file
say Active to display running progs
say CANcel to cancel a program
say ERAse to erase a program
say Edit to edit a program
say TELL to pass data to a program
say "command ?" gets you more info
end
$ FILE GAME
* Sample interactive game Program - CCS
vars ans
say You are in the Computer Room. You are
say too far from the computer to read the screen.
say There is a ferocious alien here who is armed
say to the teeth (what teeth!) - he's about to
say attack you!
again : pull ans
if (RANDOM > 400) go notmiss
say A flurry of blows but you both survive
go again
notmiss : if (ANS = KILL) go himdead
say The alien has killed you
end
himdead : say You kill the alien
$ FILE STATUS
* Sample status display Program - CCS
say State of the World at TIMENOW
say Air Pump....... AIR_PUMP
say Energy......... ENERGY
say Air Quality.... AIR_QUALITY
say Shield......... SHIELD
say Intruder Alarm. INTRUDER_ALARM
say Terminal 1..... TERMINAL1
$ FILE AIR
* Sample device setting Program - CCS
air_pump = ON
say  air pump  is now AIR_PUMP
$ FILE ALERT
* sample burglar alarm Program - CCS
intruder_alarm = ON
shield = UP
say alert level is ALERT_LEVEL
say energy level is ENERGY
$ FILE TERMINAL
* Sample interactive device setting Program - CCS
vars lstate
say Terminal 1 is currently TERMINAL1
say new state: ENABLED or DISABLED ?
pull lstate
if (LSTATE = ENABLED) terminal1 = LSTATE
if (LSTATE = DISABLED) terminal1 = LSTATE
say state now TERMINAL1
$ FILE ROBOT
* Sample simple robot program - CCS
* run when you and robot are in room with vdu
robot = go to the door
* robot should go into lift
robot = come into room please
* robot should come back into room
$ FILE LIFT
* Sample device control Program - CCS - take care!
  if (VERSION > 1) ABEND to prevent crashes
loop :  say  Lift at floor LIFT_FLOOR
  LIFT_BUTTON = OFF
  wait until LIFT_BUTTON = ON
  LIFT_DOOR = CLOSE
  if (LIFT_FLOOR = 2) go attop
  LIFT_FLOOR = 2
  go open
attop : LIFT_FLOOR = 1
open :  LIFT_DOOR = OPEN
  go loop
$ DISK ADVANCED
$ FILE BUGS
say the following feature exist in SIMPL/E
say very limited expressions
say spaces reqd between tokens
say eg labels, operators etc
say unstructured logic
say no arrays or files
say all errors cause program to abend
* True as of Feb 18th 1983
$ FILE ERROR
* Sample error trapper -CCS
vars abendnum progname junk
loop : pull abendnum  progname junk
* a program has failed, so restart it
* (don't do this if it suicided - abendnum = 998)
run PROGNAME
go loop - to trap next program
$ FILE DEBUG
vars tstate
say Trace is TRACE - new value?
pull tstate
trace = TSTATE
$ FILE VOICECONTROL
* Sample complex robot control program - CCS - take care
* Allows voice control/feedback
* say END to stop program, TEST to check if it's still there
  vars time
ack : robot_voice = Yes Master
loop :  wait until ROBOT_EAR \= #
  time = TIMENOW
  if (ROBOT_EAR = END) END
  if (ROBOT_EAR = TEST) go ack
  interpret ROBOT_EAR
  if (TIME = TIMENOW) wait 1
  go loop
$ FILE SUPERLIFT
* Sample device control Program - CCS - take care!
  vars nfloor
  if (VERSION > 1) ABEND to prevent crashes
loop :  say  Lift at floor LIFT_FLOOR
  LIFT_BUTTON = OFF
  wait until LIFT_BUTTON = ON
  LIFT_DOOR = CLOSE
  nfloor = LIFT_FLOOR
  if (NFLOOR = 4) nfloor = 0
  lift_floor = NFLOOR + 1
  LIFT_DOOR = OPEN
  go loop
$ FILE RFOLLOW
* simple program to get robot to ape what you do
* say stop to stop him
  loop : probe = ON
  if (HUMAN_HERE = 1) go doit
  wait 1
  go loop
  doit : if (ROBOT_EAR = STOP) END
  robot = HUMAN_ACT
  go doit
$ DISK ODDSANDENDS
$ FILE GETR
* simple program to get robot to computer room early on
  run lift
  lift_button = ON
  wait 4
  robot = LIFT
  robot = BUTT
  wait 1
  robot = ROOM
$ DISK EMPTY
